  "preamble": "Vocalization of the syllabic rhotic [r̩] to the vowel a. Sanskrit ṛ appears in Pali as a, i or u, often agreeing with the vowel of the following syllable (Wikipedia: kṛta > kata, tṛṣṇā > taṇhā). In all the etyma here the next syllable has a or ā. As in the r > i and r > u cells, the syllabic ṛ is filed under r.",
